{"title":"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems\">2012 AMC 12B #22</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems\">2012 AMC 10B #25</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(using_the_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (using the answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3:_Casework\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3: Casework</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bug travels from A to B along the segments in the hexagonal lattice pictured below. The segments marked with an arrow can be traveled only in the direction of the arrow, and the bug never travels the same segment more than once. How many different paths are there?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c208832b26b520d3585031acd75a37563652720.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); draw((0.0,0.0)--(1.0,1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,5.196152422706632)--(9.0,5.196152422706632)--(10.0,6.928203230275509)--(12.0,6.928203230275509)); draw((0.0,0.0)--(1.0,1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,5.196152422706632)--(9.0,5.196152422706632)--(10.0,6.928203230275509)--(12.0,6.928203230275509)); draw((3.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,0.0)--(6.0,0.0)--(7.0,1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,3.4641016151377544)--(12.0,3.464101615137755)--(13.0,5.196152422706632)--(15.0,5.196152422706632)); draw((6.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,0.0)--(12.0,0.0)--(13.0,1.7320508075688772)--(15.0,1.7320508075688776)--(16.0,3.464101615137755)--(18.0,3.4641016151377544)); draw((9.0,-5.196152422706632)--(10.0,-3.464101615137755)--(12.0,-3.464101615137755)--(13.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(15.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(16.0,0)--(18.0,0.0)--(19.0,1.7320508075688772)--(21.0,1.7320508075688767)); draw((12.0,-6.928203230275509)--(13.0,-5.196152422706632)--(15.0,-5.196152422706632)--(16.0,-3.464101615137755)--(18.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(19.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(21.0,-1.7320508075688767)--(22.0,0)); draw((0.0,-0.0)--(1.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,-5.196152422706632)--(9.0,-5.196152422706632)--(10.0,-6.928203230275509)--(12.0,-6.928203230275509)); draw((3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,-0.0)--(6.0,-0.0)--(7.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(12.0,-3.464101615137755)--(13.0,-5.196152422706632)--(15.0,-5.196152422706632)); draw((6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,-0.0)--(12.0,-0.0)--(13.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(15.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(16.0,-3.464101615137755)--(18.0,-3.4641016151377544)); draw((9.0,5.1961524)--(10.0,3.464101)--(12.0,3.46410)--(13.0,1.73205)--(15.0,1.732050)--(16.0,0)--(18.0,-0.0)--(19.0,-1.7320)--(21.0,-1.73205080)); draw((12.0,6.928203)--(13.0,5.1961524)--(15.0,5.1961524)--(16.0,3.464101615)--(18.0,3.4641016)--(19.0,1.7320508)--(21.0,1.732050)--(22.0,0)); dot((0,0)); dot((22,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),WNW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(22,0),E); filldraw((2.0,1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,1.2320508075688772)--(1.75,1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,black); filldraw((5.0,3.4641016151377544)--(4.6,2.9641016151377544)--(4.75,3.4641016151377544)--(4.6,3.9641016151377544)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,5.196152422706632)--(7.6,4.696152422706632)--(7.75,5.196152422706632)--(7.6,5.696152422706632)--cycle,black); filldraw((11.0,6.928203230275509)--(10.6,6.428203230275509)--(10.75,6.928203230275509)--(10.6,7.428203230275509)--cycle,black); filldraw((4.6,0.0)--(5.0,-0.5)--(4.85,0.0)--(5.0,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((8.0,1.732050)--(7.6,1.2320)--(7.75,1.73205)--(7.6,2.2320)--cycle,black); filldraw((11.0,3.4641016)--(10.6,2.9641016)--(10.75,3.46410161)--(10.6,3.964101)--cycle,black); filldraw((14.0,5.196152422706632)--(13.6,4.696152422706632)--(13.75,5.196152422706632)--(13.6,5.696152422706632)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,-1.732050)--(7.6,-2.232050)--(7.75,-1.7320508)--(7.6,-1.2320)--cycle,black); filldraw((10.6,0.0)--(11,-0.5)--(10.85,0.0)--(11,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((14.0,1.7320508075688772)--(13.6,1.2320508075688772)--(13.75,1.7320508075688772)--(13.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,black); filldraw((17.0,3.464101615137755)--(16.6,2.964101615137755)--(16.75,3.464101615137755)--(16.6,3.964101615137755)--cycle,black); filldraw((11.0,-3.464101615137755)--(10.6,-3.964101615137755)--(10.75,-3.464101615137755)--(10.6,-2.964101615137755)--cycle,black); filldraw((14.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(13.6,-2.2320508075688776)--(13.75,-1.7320508075688776)--(13.6,-1.2320508075688776)--cycle,black); filldraw((16.6,0)--(17,-0.5)--(16.85,0)--(17,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((20.0,1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,1.2320508075688772)--(19.75,1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,black); filldraw((14.0,-5.196152422706632)--(13.6,-5.696152422706632)--(13.75,-5.196152422706632)--(13.6,-4.696152422706632)--cycle,black); filldraw((17.0,-3.464101615137755)--(16.6,-3.964101615137755)--(16.75,-3.464101615137755)--(16.6,-2.964101615137755)--cycle,black); filldraw((20.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,-2.232050807568877)--(19.75,-1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,-1.2320508075688772)--cycle,black); filldraw((2.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,-1.2320508075688772)--(1.75,-1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,-2.232050807568877)--cycle,black); filldraw((5.0,-3.4641016)--(4.6,-2.964101)--(4.75,-3.4641)--(4.6,-3.9641016)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,-5.1961524)--(7.6,-4.6961524)--(7.75,-5.19615242)--(7.6,-5.696152422)--cycle,black); filldraw((11.0,-6.9282032)--(10.6,-6.4282032)--(10.75,-6.928203)--(10.6,-7.428203)--cycle,black);[/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"288\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23d8e86d933005c89ee6461ea9314285cf9c0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2112\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2304\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2368\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2384\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"484\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3be06871563f3956f2316f65c67714f25e5342a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); draw((0.0,0.0)--(1.0,1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,5.196152422706632)--(9.0,5.196152422706632)--(10.0,6.928203230275509)--(12.0,6.928203230275509)); draw((0.0,0.0)--(1.0,1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,5.196152422706632)--(9.0,5.196152422706632)--(10.0,6.928203230275509)--(12.0,6.928203230275509)); draw((3.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,0.0)--(6.0,0.0)--(7.0,1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,3.4641016151377544)--(12.0,3.464101615137755)--(13.0,5.196152422706632)--(15.0,5.196152422706632)); draw((6.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,0.0)--(12.0,0.0)--(13.0,1.7320508075688772)--(15.0,1.7320508075688776)--(16.0,3.464101615137755)--(18.0,3.4641016151377544)); draw((9.0,-5.196152422706632)--(10.0,-3.464101615137755)--(12.0,-3.464101615137755)--(13.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(15.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(16.0,0)--(18.0,0.0)--(19.0,1.7320508075688772)--(21.0,1.7320508075688767)); draw((12.0,-6.928203230275509)--(13.0,-5.196152422706632)--(15.0,-5.196152422706632)--(16.0,-3.464101615137755)--(18.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(19.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(21.0,-1.7320508075688767)--(22.0,0)); draw((0.0,-0.0)--(1.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,-5.196152422706632)--(9.0,-5.196152422706632)--(10.0,-6.928203230275509)--(12.0,-6.928203230275509)); draw((3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,-0.0)--(6.0,-0.0)--(7.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(12.0,-3.464101615137755)--(13.0,-5.196152422706632)--(15.0,-5.196152422706632)); draw((6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,1.7320508075688772)--(10.0,-0.0)--(12.0,-0.0)--(13.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(15.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(16.0,-3.464101615137755)--(18.0,-3.4641016151377544)); draw((9.0,5.1961524)--(10.0,3.464101)--(12.0,3.46410)--(13.0,1.73205)--(15.0,1.732050)--(16.0,0)--(18.0,-0.0)--(19.0,-1.7320)--(21.0,-1.73205080)); draw((12.0,6.928203)--(13.0,5.1961524)--(15.0,5.1961524)--(16.0,3.464101615)--(18.0,3.4641016)--(19.0,1.7320508)--(21.0,1.732050)--(22.0,0)); dot((0,0)); dot((22,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),WNW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(22,0),E); filldraw((2.0,1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,1.2320508075688772)--(1.75,1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,red); filldraw((5.0,3.4641016151377544)--(4.6,2.9641016151377544)--(4.75,3.4641016151377544)--(4.6,3.9641016151377544)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,5.196152422706632)--(7.6,4.696152422706632)--(7.75,5.196152422706632)--(7.6,5.696152422706632)--cycle,blue); filldraw((11.0,6.928203230275509)--(10.6,6.428203230275509)--(10.75,6.928203230275509)--(10.6,7.428203230275509)--cycle,black); filldraw((4.6,0.0)--(5.0,-0.5)--(4.85,0.0)--(5.0,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((8.0,1.732050)--(7.6,1.2320)--(7.75,1.73205)--(7.6,2.2320)--cycle,blue); filldraw((11.0,3.4641016)--(10.6,2.9641016)--(10.75,3.46410161)--(10.6,3.964101)--cycle,black); filldraw((14.0,5.196152422706632)--(13.6,4.696152422706632)--(13.75,5.196152422706632)--(13.6,5.696152422706632)--cycle,green); filldraw((8.0,-1.732050)--(7.6,-2.232050)--(7.75,-1.7320508)--(7.6,-1.2320)--cycle,blue); filldraw((10.6,0.0)--(11,-0.5)--(10.85,0.0)--(11,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((14.0,1.7320508075688772)--(13.6,1.2320508075688772)--(13.75,1.7320508075688772)--(13.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,green); filldraw((17.0,3.464101615137755)--(16.6,2.964101615137755)--(16.75,3.464101615137755)--(16.6,3.964101615137755)--cycle,black); filldraw((11.0,-3.464101615137755)--(10.6,-3.964101615137755)--(10.75,-3.464101615137755)--(10.6,-2.964101615137755)--cycle,black); filldraw((14.0,-1.7320508075688776)--(13.6,-2.2320508075688776)--(13.75,-1.7320508075688776)--(13.6,-1.2320508075688776)--cycle,green); filldraw((16.6,0)--(17,-0.5)--(16.85,0)--(17,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((20.0,1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,1.2320508075688772)--(19.75,1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,orange); filldraw((14.0,-5.196152422706632)--(13.6,-5.696152422706632)--(13.75,-5.196152422706632)--(13.6,-4.696152422706632)--cycle,green); filldraw((17.0,-3.464101615137755)--(16.6,-3.964101615137755)--(16.75,-3.464101615137755)--(16.6,-2.964101615137755)--cycle,black); filldraw((20.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,-2.232050807568877)--(19.75,-1.7320508075688772)--(19.6,-1.2320508075688772)--cycle,orange); filldraw((2.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,-1.2320508075688772)--(1.75,-1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,-2.232050807568877)--cycle,red); filldraw((5.0,-3.4641016)--(4.6,-2.964101)--(4.75,-3.4641)--(4.6,-3.9641016)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,-5.1961524)--(7.6,-4.6961524)--(7.75,-5.19615242)--(7.6,-5.696152422)--cycle,blue); filldraw((11.0,-6.9282032)--(10.6,-6.4282032)--(10.75,-6.928203)--(10.6,-7.428203)--cycle,black);[/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"288\" />\n</p><p>We can count the number of ways to get from each set of only solid arrows to the next set; if we pass any set, we can't go to points behind that set. We break the diagram up like this to ensure that we don't overcount; otherwise, we would be able to return through the outlined white arrow to previous points, making the casework very difficult. Then, we find the total number of cases by multiplying the number of ways we can get from each of the sections to the next one.\n</p><p>There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way to get to any of the red arrows. From the first (top) red arrow, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to each of the first and the second (top 2) blue arrows; from the second (bottom) red arrow, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to each of the first and the second blue arrows. So, by symmetry there are in total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get from any of the red arrows to any of the blue arrows. \n</p><p>From each of the first and second blue arrows, there are respectively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to each of the first and the second green arrows; from each of the third and the fourth blue arrows, there are respectively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to each of the first and the second green arrows. Therefore, as there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to go from the start to blue, and another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b403ba308e3196a037e3a7e6c99e5bd1b7cf1202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+4+8+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> ways to go from blue to green, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to the green arrows.\n</p><p>Finally, from each of the first and second green arrows, there are respectively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to the first orange arrow; from each of the third and the fourth green arrows, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get to the first orange arrow. Therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b5a702ffb0ec6c3de032bddd40123855634084f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 \\cdot (2+2+3+3) = 1200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"18\" /> ways to get to each of the orange arrows, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4208d59c57ee9a549ff172069df39fac811d562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> ways to get to the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4d570fd87834da0fd1e8d5d0d12699dd3766aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"81\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28using_the_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(using_the_answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (using the answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (using the answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d332ccfc90a148821164dfbe55cbdac163baf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(6cm); draw((0.0,0.0)--(1.0,1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,5.196152422706632)--(9.0,5.196152422706632)); draw((0.0,0.0)--(1.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(3.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(6.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,-5.196152422706632)--(9.0,-5.196152422706632)); draw((6.0,-3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,-1.7320508075688772)); draw((4.0, 0.0)--(6.0,0.0)); draw((6.0,3.4641016151377544)--(7.0,1.7320508075688772)--(9.0,1.7320508075688772)); draw((3.0,1.7320508075688772)--(4.0,-0.0)--(3.0,-1.7320508075688772), red); draw((7.0,1.7320508075688772)--(6.0,-0.0)--(7.0,-1.7320508075688772), blue);   dot((0,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),WNW); filldraw((2.0,1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,1.2320508075688772)--(1.75,1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,2.232050807568877)--cycle,red); filldraw((5.0,3.4641016151377544)--(4.6,2.9641016151377544)--(4.75,3.4641016151377544)--(4.6,3.9641016151377544)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,5.196152422706632)--(7.6,4.696152422706632)--(7.75,5.196152422706632)--(7.6,5.696152422706632)--cycle,blue); filldraw((4.6,0.0)--(5.0,-0.5)--(4.85,0.0)--(5.0,0.5)--cycle,white); filldraw((8.0,1.732050)--(7.6,1.2320)--(7.75,1.73205)--(7.6,2.2320)--cycle,blue); filldraw((8.0,-1.732050)--(7.6,-2.232050)--(7.75,-1.7320508)--(7.6,-1.2320)--cycle,blue); filldraw((2.0,-1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,-1.2320508075688772)--(1.75,-1.7320508075688772)--(1.6,-2.232050807568877)--cycle,red); filldraw((5.0,-3.4641016)--(4.6,-2.964101)--(4.75,-3.4641)--(4.6,-3.9641016)--cycle,black); filldraw((8.0,-5.1961524)--(7.6,-4.6961524)--(7.75,-5.19615242)--(7.6,-5.696152422)--cycle,blue); [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"285\" />\n</p><p>For every blue arrow, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82a0ae3d5267c1879cc6b0c99ad66ed85d29f23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> ways to reach it without using the reverse arrow since the bug can choose any of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red arrows to pass through and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> black arrows to pass through.  If the bug passes through the white arrow, the red arrow that the bug travels through must be the closest to the first black arrow. Otherwise, the bug will have to travel through both red segments, which is impossible because now there is no path to take after the bug emerges from the reverse arrow.  Similarly, with the blue segments, the second black arrow taken must be the one that is closest to the blue arrow that was taken.  Also, it is trivial that the two black arrows taken must be different.  Therefore, if the reverse arrow is taken, the blue arrow taken determines the entire path and there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> path for every arrow.  Since the bug cannot return once it takes a blue arrow, the answer must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4d570fd87834da0fd1e8d5d0d12699dd3766aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"81\" height=\"28\" /> is the only answer that is.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3:_Casework\">Solution 3: Casework</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3: Casework\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The main thing to notice is that, if the bug does not go backwards, then every vertical set of arrows can be used, as the bug could travel straight downwards and then use any arrow to continue right.\n</p><p>Note: The motivation is quite weird so follow my numbers as they start from the left (point A) and go right (point B).\n</p><p>Case 1: Bug does not go backwards.\n</p><p>The number of cases for this is just each vertical set of arrows multiplied to each other (if you don't understand where I'm coming from, try to understand where these numbers come from!)\n</p><p>And so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dac983a7586b6fb905049ef423ce0c32f8739edb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot2\\cdot4\\cdot4\\cdot4\\cdot2\\cdot2 = 2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"17\" /> cases.\n</p><p>Case 2: The bug goes backwards once, either at the first arrow or third arrow.\n</p><p>Here, we have to count the fact that there is a horizontal midline that the bug could not cross, or otherwise it would be stepping on the same edge twice.\nBack on first arrow: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/0292b067efcfef3e681c227aac4973bfca8460aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot1\\cdot2\\cdot4\\cdot4\\cdot2\\cdot2 = 2^{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" /> cases.\nThe third arrow is the same. \n</p><p>Case 3: The bug goes backwards once, at the second arrow.\n</p><p>Same thing as above, except since there are 4 arrows in the vertical set (plus one for the backwards arrow), then the calculations are a bit different.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd31d57b3ffab2a1f91a1dfabd5ef854f1335e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot2\\cdot4\\cdot1\\cdot2\\cdot4\\cdot2\\cdot2 = 2^{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"17\" /> cases.\n</p><p>Notice that the first and third back arrows decrease the number of cases by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and the second back arrow decreases the number of cases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e68ad31d12ba3d14b80a9341ee44e6238555124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />. Hence,\n</p><p>1st + 2nd = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc77519ee6bab163b1aa195a3ba88718d414aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>2nd + 3rd = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc77519ee6bab163b1aa195a3ba88718d414aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>1st + 3rd = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a91d92ded08453fe4662a56223d382b4cba6aa35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>1st + 2nd + 3rd = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7f45c960c681827d5d03d7b3c30811d3bfd77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>And so the number of cases in total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0aa885ed77e73042f44ae80bf32c535917d018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10} + 2^9 + 2^8 + 2^8 + 2^7 + 2^7 + 2^6 + 2^5 = 1024 + 512 + 256 + 256 + 128 + 128 + 64 + 32 = \\boxed{2400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"757\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~IronicNinja ~LaTeX help with Roy2020\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012amc10b/270\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012amc10b/270</a>\n</p><p>~dolphin7\n</p><p>(Direct Youtube Link)\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SE3hYHHYqhk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SE3hYHHYqhk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B\">2012 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolv